cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this file) and the
  accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
title: >-
  JayQuery: per-channel differential privacy in cross-institution split
  vertical federated learning
abstract: >-
  A two-silo split vertical federated learning system that carries three
  differential privacy mechanisms at once, cut-layer Gaussian noise on each
  silo's embeddings, DP-SGD on the coordinator's top model, and prior-based
  randomized response on the labels, each with its own accountant and an
  explicitly stated neighboring relation. Includes elliptic-curve private set
  intersection over ristretto255, an embedding-inversion attack with a
  noise-matched learned inverse, loss-threshold membership inference, and the
  sweep and analysis tooling used to produce the reported results.
